Pre-existing, unrelated to NEARS-2660: every request in this QA session emitted a
paired WARN/ERROR OTel-export-failure block (circuit breaker open->half_open->open
for metrics + traces, then "[FAIL] OpenTelemetry export failed (telemetry batch
dropped)") because the local OpenObserve collector (localhost:5080) is not running
in this dev environment. 66 occurrences across this session alone.

Sample:
[2026-08-31 01:58:20] production.WARNING: [WARN] OTel export circuit breaker open -> half_open (signal=metrics) {"trace_id":"48b4d2cef9ffea020d7a33aa743db035","correlation_id":"aa3b491d-da46-4b7a-91a4-87838a4f95c5","signal":"metrics","from":"open","to":"half_open"}
[2026-08-31 01:58:20] production.ERROR: [FAIL] OpenTelemetry export failed (telemetry batch dropped): Export failure {"trace_id":"48b4d2cef9ffea020d7a33aa743db035","correlation_id":"aa3b491d-da46-4b7a-91a4-87838a4f95c5","suppressed_since_last":0,"source":"OpenTelemetry\\Contrib\\Otlp\\MetricExporter","signal":"metrics","otlp_endpoint":"localhost:5080/api/default","error_type":"GuzzleHttp\\Exception\\ConnectException","error_message":"cURL error 7: Failed to connect to localhost:5080 after 0 ms: Could not connect to server (see https://curl.se/libcurl/c/libcurl-errors.html) for http://localhost:5080/api/default/v1/metrics"}

Not caused by this ticket's diff (PlaceNewOrder.php only). Almost certainly a
local-dev-environment gap (OpenObserve/OTel collector not started), not a code
defect, but flagged since it floods laravel.log on every request and could mask
a genuine [FAIL] line in a future grep-scoped QA pass if the noise ratio grows.
